{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"color","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartsymbol\/color"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPartSymbol/color":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartsymbol\/color","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol\/color","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"title":"color","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPartSymbol":{"title":"MXLPartSymbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartsymbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol","abstract":[{"text":"The part-symbol type indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score; brace is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default value. The top-staff and bottom-staff attributes are used when the brace does not extend across the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entire part. For example, in a 3-staff organ part, the top-staff will typically be 1 for the right hand, while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the bottom-staff will typically be 2 for the left hand. Staff 3 for the pedals is usually outside the brace.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default, the presence of a part-symbol element that does not extend across the entire part also indicates a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corresponding change in the common barlines within a part.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"}}}